        "# H3 Infinite v1.4 — Native Masked AV Continuation (v1.4)\n\nUse this workflow for **Clip 2 and every later clip**.\n\n**Requires a current ComfyUI build containing native PR #15375 H3 AV-mask support.**\n\n1. Load the full AV latent saved by the previous clip, including its `handover` metadata.\n2. Optionally connect a new **Last Frame** and one or more **Qwen References**.\n3. Enter the next prompt.\n4. Recommended defaults: `masked_context_frames = 39`, `audio_feather_ticks = 0`, `Duration Mode = Net New Content`, `Audio Tail Carryover = Full Previous Tail`.\n5. Queue. The video context is copied from the freeze/brightness-safe source window and hard-protected with the native mask.\n6. The audio context starts at the same source point but can remain protected through the previous clip's real audio ending, preserving dialogue/phoneme endings beyond the earlier visual cut.\n7. Save the new full latent under the next manual clip index and repeat.\n\nThe previous latent is **not** reconstructed as RoPE/guide keyframes and is not a Qwen Picture. It lives directly inside the new target latent."
      ],
      "color": "#1f4d3b",
      "bgcolor": "#2c6b52"
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -930,
        40
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 23,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Models & optimization",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Model setup\nUse the **same H3 diffusion model, Qwen encoder, Video VAE, Audio VAE and resolution** as the previous clip.\n\nSageAttention is optional. Changing core model/VAE settings between clips can break continuity or latent compatibility.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1550,
        800
      ],
      "size": [
        430,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 24,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Load previous latent",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Load Previous AV Latent + Handover\nLoads the complete sampler-output **video + audio latent** and its saved Auto Handover metadata.\n\nv1.4 needs both:\n- the latent supplies the actual video/audio tensors,\n- `handover` supplies the freeze/brightness-safe visual boundary selected for that accepted clip.\n\nKeep manual clip indices predictable: generating Clip 2 loads slot 1, Clip 3 loads slot 2, etc."
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1080,
        990
      ],
      "size": [
        720,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 25,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Optional endpoint & Qwen References",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Image inputs and Picture mapping\n**Last Frame is optional.** When connected it is the new temporal endpoint / quality-reset keyframe for this continuation clip.\n\n**Qwen Reference 1** is optional Qwen-only image guidance. Connecting it reveals Qwen Reference 2, then 3, and so on up to nine.\n\nThe previous AV latent supplies temporal history directly and is **not** decoded into a Qwen Picture.\n\nExamples:\n- Last Frame + Ref 1 -> `Picture 1 = Last Frame`, `Picture 2 = Qwen Reference 1`\n- no Last Frame + Ref 1 + Ref 2 -> `Picture 1 = Qwen Reference 1`, `Picture 2 = Qwen Reference 2`\n\nUse the node's `picture_map` output / console log as the authoritative mapping for the current graph.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -240,
        1080
      ],
      "size": [
        680,
        390
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 26,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Continue from Latent v1.4",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Native Masked AV — v1.4 defaults\n- `masked_context_frames = 39` — recommended safe video context (~1.625 s). Larger exact choices remain 90 / 141 / 192 frames.\n- `audio_feather_ticks = 0` — recommended hard audio protection, especially for speech.\n- `Duration Mode = Net New Content` — **new default**. Duration means approximately how much newly generated visible video remains after the protected video head is removed. This samples a longer total latent and therefore increases sampling time versus `Total Generation`.\n- `Audio Tail Carryover = Full Previous Tail` — **new default**. Video still ends at the safe visual handover, while original audio may stay protected through the previous clip's actual end. This helps preserve word/phoneme endings that continue into visually discarded freeze/brightness frames.\n\nUse `Match Video Handover` to reproduce validated audio behavior for A/B testing.\n\nImportant limitation: audio carryover can only preserve audio that already exists in the previous latent. If the original clip itself ends mid-word, H3 still has to invent what comes after it."
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        390,
        830
      ],
      "size": [
        770,
        310
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 27,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Sampling settings",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Sampling\nUse the same sampler, scheduler, Sigma Shift and general H3 settings as the first clip unless you have a specific reason to change them.\n\nThe seed may be randomized per clip; continuity comes from the direct latent context and endpoint conditioning, not from reusing the same noise seed.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1580,
        1020
      ],
      "size": [
        640,
        350
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 28,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Auto Handover",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### One safe video boundary, independent audio tail\nv1.4 keeps the proven video logic:\n1. Detect the unusable FL2VA landing tail.\n2. Snap the safe visual cutoff backward to the latest exact Masked-AV video boundary.\n3. `Stitch Ready` cuts the previous video at that exact boundary.\n4. The next Continue protects the safe video context ending at exactly the same boundary.\n\nAudio is now allowed to continue farther than that visual boundary. This deliberately separates **where the picture is safe to cut** from **where useful speech actually ends**."
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1230,
        790
      ],
      "size": [
        350,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 29,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Save next AV Latent",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Save the next full AV latent\nSave the sampler's complete video + audio latent together with Auto Handover **and `actual_head_context_frames`**. The Save node stores that head length in the `.safetensors` metadata so the clip can later be stitched automatically without reopening this generation graph.\n\nKeep one numbered prefix (`clip_00001`, `clip_00002`, ...) for the whole chain and set each clip index manually. This stable manual behavior is intentionally retained in v1.4.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2030,
        560
      ],
      "size": [
        850,
        360
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 30,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Output / Stitch modes",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Output / Stitch\n**Stitch Ready** — intermediate segment. Removes the complete reused Masked-AV head plus the detector trim; it also handles soft final-state tails dynamically and otherwise uses the conservative 11-frame Balanced fallback.\n\n**Final Clip** — removes only the reused head and keeps the final segment's complete ending.\n\nWhen a previous freeze tail was removed, the v1.4 Seamless Join automatically shifts its crossfade anchor to the **time-corresponding earlier position inside the next protected 39-frame head**. The protected head itself is still completely removed from the final timeline."
      ],
      "color": "#66511f",
      "bgcolor": "#8a6d28"
    }
